## What
Create a 'Devolved nations' component for linking to guidance for other nations and then update it accross GOV.UK 

## Why
- The current banner for linking to guidance for other nations is not accessible enough because the links have no context. 
- There are approximately 40k instances (currently created with the important metadata component) in Whitehall alone
- WCAG fail

https://trello.com/c/WVrZ35zt/793-dev-implementation-of-devolved-nations-task

## Anything else

Example(s) of where the original issue exists:
- https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/firefighters-pension-scheme-membership-data-england-2010-11
- https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/code-for-sustainable-homes-and-energy-performance-of-buildings-data-march-2012
- https://www.gov.uk/guidance/red-amber-and-green-list-rules-for-entering-england

## API proposal

## High level
The 'Devolved nations' component accepts a list of objects for each 'nation'. And each object allows for two key/value pairs:
- applicable (must be `true` to be included)
- alternative_url - the alternative URL for other guidance.
The default heading level is `h2` unless otherwise specified.

## Example API calls
### Basic use
```
<%= render "govuk_publishing_components/components/devolved_nations", {
  national_applicability: {
    england: {
      applicable: true
    }
  }
} %>
```
<img src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/87758239/130644042-64eaeaea-e317-4340-9c58-5045c12820a2.png" width="400">

### Applies to two nations
```
  national_applicability: {
    england: {
      applicable: true
    },
    wales: {
      applicable: true
    }
  }
} %>
```
<img src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/87758239/130644237-03647cbd-ac9f-4034-8bd5-45664801497a.png" width="400">

### Applies to one nation individual guidance available
```
<%= render "govuk_publishing_components/components/devolved_nations", {
  national_applicability: {
    england: {
      applicable: true
    },
    northern_ireland: {
      applicable: false,
      alternative_url: "/"
    },
    scotland: {
      applicable: false,
      alternative_url: "/"
    },
    wales: {
      applicable: false,
      alternative_url: "/"
    }
  }
} %>
```
